HOW TO READ
========================================================================================================
  Look for ONE row where the GRUNT effect approaches the capture's +11.6 AND noon/cut
  approaches -10.6 AND the ramp rms drops. All three at the SAME (A0, K), or it is not
  evidence — taking the best cell from each column certifies nothing.
  If such a row exists at A0 well below 20, then circuit.md's 20-30 is a PRIOR that this
  unit's own GRUNT corners contradict, and the session-15 rejection of clipA0 = 8.2 was
  the optimiser being right for a reason nobody had measured. That does NOT license
  shipping a low A0 on this evidence alone — it licenses MEASURING the GRUNT corners
  bleed-free (harmonics carry no clean bleed) and re-deriving A0 from them properly.
